%-------------------- Abstract & Declaration ----------------------------
\begin{titlepage}
	\begin{abstract}
		The evolution toward 6G mobile networks has catalyzed the AI-RAN paradigm, envisioning a profound convergence of Radio Access Network (RAN) infrastructure and artificial intelligence workloads. Modern GPU-accelerated base stations frequently exhibit significant, temporally bursty spare compute capacity. The central challenge addressed in this research is how to safely harness this underutilized edge compute for latency-critical AI inference tasks without compromising the stringent Service Level Agreements (SLAs) of primary telecommunication functions. This project proposes the design and evaluation of a cloud-native, multi-tenant scheduling architecture. Adopting a strict ``RAN-first'' operational philosophy, it utilizes advanced workload isolation to dynamically multiplex containerized AI inference into the distributed unit (DU), guaranteeing zero degradation to network reliability.
	\end{abstract}

	\vspace*{2cm}

